# oracle: pair_style lj/long/coul/long cut long 8 10 with the default Coulomb table (pair_modify table 12) on bonded chains (special_bonds charmm: the special-bond correction of the table branch), Ewald Coulomb
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.6e-14, atoms 3.4e-14 (the Coulomb table at the float rsq, before: 9.1e-9).
# oracle-inputs: w10charmmfsw_chains.data
units           real
atom_style      full
read_data       w10charmmfsw_chains.data
special_bonds   charmm
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 300.0 1.5
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 50.0 110.0
pair_style      lj/long/coul/long cut long 8.0 10.0
kspace_style    ewald 1.0e-5
kspace_modify   gewald 0.28 kmax/ewald 7 7 7
pair_coeff      1 1 0.1 3.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.15 3.2
timestep        1.0
velocity        all set 0.001 0.0 0.0 units box
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl ecoul ebond eangle elong etotal press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             40
